mentor: Looks like Operator was right, Gardener.
mentor: Moonsanto's a major supplier to large scale farms around the world.
mentor: They're also famously litigious ---
mentor: If they were the ones who made this forest-choking strangler fig, you might find yourself in court for tracking its seeds out of here on your shoes.
mentor: Patented...
mentor: Everything's goddamn patented.
mentor: But this doesn't make any sense...
mentor: They make herbicide resistant beans, not parasitic epiphytes.
mentor: What reason could they possibly have to let this thing loose out here?
mentor: ...
mentor: If I know them, they're creating a problem to sell the solution.
mentor: But this...
mentor: They turned a goddamn keystone species into a threat of mass-deforestation.
mentor: If the solution they're selling is a *stronger* herbicide again, I swear...
